Package: flickos-menu
Architecture: all
# python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1: the menu, GTK 3 so it
# follows the Arc theme. labwc: a tap of Super is labwc's onRelease keybind,
# and the daemon sees Super because labwc sends modifiers to every client.
# procps: pkill, how the panel button and labwc reach the daemon.
# Quick Settings runs the programs that own its settings (nmcli,
# flickos-control, flick-tiler, flickos-phone, wpctl, brightnessctl); a
# control whose program is missing is left out, so none is a Depends here.
# The phone popup reads flickos-phone actions (1.16) and mute, and state
# ringing (1.17). Older than that, the popup can't draw.
# python3-gi-cairo: a window fading out passes clicks to the one below (an
# empty input region); flickos-shortcuts has it already.
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         python3-gi-cairo,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1,
         labwc,
         procps,
         ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: flickos-phone (<< 1.17)
Description: start menu and Quick Settings for the FlickOS labwc session
 A two-column start menu for the panel's apps button: pinned apps, all apps
 by category, search, the user's folders, Settings, and lock, log out,
 restart and shut down. A tap of the Super (Windows) key opens it too.
 .
 It is the apps button's default. Settings > Desktop Layout & Style can
 switch the button back to the fuzzel launcher. While it is off, nothing of
 it runs.
 .
 Quick Settings, off by default, opens from the panel's volume and battery
 icons and Super+A: switches for Wi-Fi, Do Not Disturb, night light, tiling
 and the phone, sliders for volume and brightness, and the battery.
 .
 The phone popup opens from the panel's phone button while the phone
 connection is on: the phone, what can be sent, a ringing call, and what
 recently arrived. The button keeps its menu when this package is removed.
